### ssl-api-controller-basis-warrant.md
# Canonical own-coordinate projection warrant

Status: source-warranted partial manifest staged on an owned private candidate; not published.

Primary NSM chart v20 identifies the elementary GOOD, BAD, BIG and SMALL lexical units through exact source identities, independently of all ordinary same-spelled dictionary senses. GSE.curation.schema.BIPOLAR_PAIRS explicitly identifies GOOD/BAD and BIG/SMALL; the existing representation uses the named positive coordinate and its negative pole. Consequently these four exact canonical identities warrant GOOD=+1, GOOD=-1, BIG=+1 and BIG=-1 respectively. This is definitional basis correspondence, not inference from frame participants, spelling or model agreement.

The source-native headings, source file hashes, definition kinds, unit IDs and candidate identities are checked for each projection and the complete observations are retained. The existing explicit entry-ID partial-anchor manifest format, resolver, storage, catalog refresh and full ordinary writer preflight are used. No other coordinate is zeroed; only existing approved joint closure may entail further values. No ordinary WordNet or Wiktionary sense inherits this anchor. Existing native chart source_structure records stay unchanged.

The complete private candidate must pass full ordinary replay before typed teaching, and the joint revision must pass full preflight and postflight before publication. Native source assertions, model-prefix history and independent rule admission remain separately attributable. These four exact own-coordinate projections are not four complete lexical signatures, do not establish semantic foundation completeness and do not by themselves satisfy the usable-workload gate.


